  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana - Set-up toilet paper factory</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan, GoodRoll Africa B.V. is able to set up a factory together with the local subsidiary for the production of toilet paper in Ghana. GoodRoll BV is a social enterprise from Amsterdam that started in 2017 with the creative packaging of toilet paper through a social workshop, with an emphasis on sustainability and online sales. For the further expansion of the turnover and result, and to pull more people out of poverty, they are going to realize a toilet roll factory in Ghana. For the paper, no wood pulp is used as a base, but bamboo fibers. Bamboo is abundantly present in Ghana and has hardly any commercial value, while as a raw material it is more biologically responsible than wood.The investment is mainly in machines for the benefit of the factory. The factory is a production line of dozens of devices to convert bamboo into custom-cut toilet rolls.The mission of the entrepreneurs for Ghana (and rather East Africa) is also to use 50% of the profits for the construction of sanitary facilities, which in many places is seriously lacking there. There is a separate foundation for this, The GoodRoll Foundation.The company has received a contribution in the DGGF TA programme for a feasibility study into the exploitation of bamboo as a basic raw material.</narrative>
  </description>
